#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""openrouter-cli - reach non-Anthropic models from a Claude Code session.

Claude Code resolves a `model:` name against api.anthropic.com, so there is no
frontmatter route to another vendor. model-router used to supply one by
redirecting ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, but that redirect hard-disables Remote Control.
This CLI is the shell-out alternative: Remote Control keeps working, and the
OpenRouter families stay reachable.

    openrouter-cli models                 # configured models
    openrouter-cli models --check         # ...cross-checked against the catalogue
    openrouter-cli drift                  # every configured slug vs the catalogue
    openrouter-cli refresh                # rank via Epoch ECI (+ AA if keyed)
    openrouter-cli ask glm "question"     # one model
    openrouter-cli fusion "question"      # panel in parallel + chair synthesis
    openrouter-cli council roster --check # is the seated roster still the best?
    openrouter-cli council refresh --apply# re-pick every seat from the indices
    openrouter-cli council ask "question" # the standing multi-family council

`fusion` is the primitive for multi-family work: OpenRouter dispatches the
panel server-side and the response names consensus, contradictions and
unique_insights per member, so a collapsed panel is visible rather than silent.

Attribution, required by the data licences: intelligence scores come from
Artificial Analysis (artificialanalysis.ai) and the Epoch Capabilities Index
(Epoch AI, CC-BY).
"""

from __future__ import annotations

